# Bakable and LayeredFS (both, always)

A playable patch is unfinished if it only lands in one of these. Do **both**.

| Path | What “done” means |
|------|-------------------|
| **Bake / CIA** | Drop CIA injects it. `code.bin` → `deploy_name_input_en.py` → `release/name_input_code.bin`. `img.bin` chrome → `tools/deploy_*_en.py` hooked from `rebuild_bake_img.py`. TRB → overlay / bake TRB step. |
| **LayeredFS** | Apply to live Azahar mods (`%AppData%\Azahar\load\mods\00040000000F4E00\` or `NLPP_AZAHAR_USER_DIR`). `exefs/code.bin` and/or `romfs/img.bin` as appropriate. `--deploy-azahar` or the feature `deploy_*` script. Backup `*.bak_pre_<feature>`. |

## Do

- Hook bake **and** offer a LayeredFS deploy in the same change (Message Speed: `patch_message_speed.py` in `deploy_name_input_en.py` **and** `--deploy-azahar`).
- If LayeredFS `code.bin` / `img.bin` is missing, say so; still wire the deploy. Do not skip bake because Azahar is unset.
- After `code.bin` edits: rebuild `name_input_code.bin` (`rebuild_bake_img.py --skip-pack` is enough when the bake stamp already matches).

## Don’t

- Azahar-only LayeredFS as the ship path (no CIA inject) — banned; see `from-scratch-bake`.
- Bake-only with no LayeredFS apply path (untestable in the emulator loop).
- Assume an existing `release/name_input_code.bin` already contains a new `code.bin` patch — bake **deletes and rewrites** it from vanilla.

Details: `technical.md` §15.5 (bake) and §21 (Message Speed example).
